---
// Ryan Holt's maker note for Tome Keeper, shared between the homepage and /tomekeeper/.
---
<p>
  Hi, I'm Ryan, and I made Tome Keeper. I move a lot, so lugging around shelves of hardcover tabletop RPG books has
  never really worked for me, even though I still love how a real book feels in your hands. I tried plenty of PDF
  readers for my library, and most of them felt like office tools. Clunky toolbars sat over the artwork, and flipping
  between rulebooks during a game was a chore.
</p>
<p>
  I built Tome Keeper so you can enjoy the full-page art, spreads, and stories in your books without all that clutter
  in the way, and still carry your whole library on one device. When it's time to prep a session or run a game, the
  tools are right there in the corner. You can clip rules, maps, or whole pages from different books onto one Table and
  arrange them in a way that makes sense for you and your players.
</p>
